[232.862085, "i", "cat > /app/bloat_memo.md <<'MD'\n# Monthly table maintenance review memo\n\nAudit date: 2026-09-01. The audit computes size class from `total_pages` (>=500 large, <500 small), computes bloat ratio as `dead_pages / total_pages` with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and applies finding precedence autovacuum, bloat, stale.\n\n## Non-compliant findings\n\n- T-13 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, which overrides the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 50 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.50 would face the stale tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-17 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, overriding the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 50 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.40 would face the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-27 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 46 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.38 is over "]
[232.862509, "i", "the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-04 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 45 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.10 is under the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-21 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum, even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 45 days, and ratio 0.20 would be over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-26 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-30 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-36 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not the legacy days_since_analyze field), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-40 is STALE_STATISTICS"]
[232.862804, "o", "cat > /app/bloat_memo.md <<'MD'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rthe tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-04 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 45 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.10 is under the tightene"]
[232.863044, "i", " because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 35 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.05 is under the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-42 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-45 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 33 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and round-half-up makes 155/1000 ratio 0.16, which is over the tightened cap 0.15.\n- T-10 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and its approved active reindex is still valid through 2026-09-15, so ratio 0.21 is exempt from the bloat cap 0.15.\n- T-16 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days, its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened c"]
[232.863311, "o", "d cap 0.15.\r\n- T-21 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum, even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 45 days, and ratio 0.20 would be over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-26 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-30 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-36 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not the legacy days_since_analyze field), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-40 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 35 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.05 is under the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-42 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEED"]
[232.863555, "i", "ap 0.15.\n- T-19 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, round-half-up makes 405/1000 ratio 0.41, which is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-06 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, ratio 0.25 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-14 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large (ignoring the export small label), ratio 0.40 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-18 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, round-half-up makes 205/1000 ratio 0.21, which is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-20 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum, even though total_pages 1000 computes to large and ratio 0.10 is under the cap 0.2.\n- T-29 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, and ratio 0.25 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-35 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 500 computes to large, ratio 0.22 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-37 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED bec"]
[232.863701, "o", "ED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-45 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 33 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and round-half-up makes 155/1000 ratio 0.16, which is over the tightened cap 0.15.\r\n- T-10 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and its approved active reindex is still valid through 2026-09-15, so ratio 0.21 is exempt from the bloat cap 0.15.\r\n- T-16 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days, its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened c\u001b[?2004h> "]
[232.863831, "i", "ause total_pages 1000 computes to large, its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, and ratio 0.25 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-39 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum, even though total_pages 1000 computes to large and ratio 0.05 is under the cap 0.2.\n- T-44 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 600 computes to large, ignoring the medium trap in the export size_class, and ratio 0.83 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-08 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large (ignoring the export small label), ratio 0.45 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-02 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, ratio 0.35 is over the cap 0.2.\n- T-03 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, which overrides the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large and ratio 0.15 is under the cap 0.2.\n- T-05 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, its reindex is unapproved (approved=False), and ratio 0.55 is over "]
[232.864064, "i", "the cap 0.2.\n- T-11 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, which overrides the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large and ratio 0.41 is over the cap 0.2.\n\n## Active maintenance and cap-equality notes\n\nT-28 has an approved active reindex valid through 2026-09-15, so its bloat check is exempt and the finding is none. A computed bloat ratio that exactly equals its size-class cap is compliant because the policy flags only ratios strictly greater than the cap; for example, T-32 at 0.40 equals its small cap 0.40, while T-12, T-15, and T-34 at 0.20 equal the large cap 0.20.\nMD\n"]
